I'm only prepared to receive these  migrants that are coming or that are  expected to come this year compared to  other countries with rich country with  high living conditions so I think it's  our obligation to help these help these  people if you look to the situation in  Syria it's obvious under which  conditions these people had to leave  their country so this is our first  obligation on the other side it's also  clear that other member states of the  European have to take their part of the  shear so we have to do two things first  of all help the people here make sure  that they can work as soon as possible  make sure that they learn German as soon  as possible and on the other side it's  also clear we have to talk to our  European friends this is a European goal  that we all have to put our part into it  but do you think a European solution is  at all possible when you consider that  different countries have very different  interests in all this it's good that the  Chancellor finally spoke out towards  that direction and made clear that this  is a European challenge for all of us  but there's a lot to do I mean just to  give you two examples cosa was still not  recognized as an independent state by  five member states of the European Union  look at Macedonia Greece still refuses  to recognize the name of that country so  how can you have stability in a region  wherein one member state does not  recognize the name of the other state  and where five member states do not  recognize one independent state there so  that doesn't help to have an investment  friendly climate to have growth jobs in  those countries and of course we also  have to put pressure on those countries  I mean I decided in the German Bundestag  about laws in in Greece and the members  of the Parliament in Greece just have to  follow what was decided in other  Parliament's so if we can put that kind  of pressure to Greece why can't we talk  to those countries and at the same time  make clear you have to fight against  corruption you have to make sure that  your citizens have better living  conditions in particular the Roma  citizens have living conditions that fit  to a country that wants to join the  European Union in the last few hours  we've seen a lot of migrants trying to  come to Germany from Hungary how big a  problem is this for Germany  I mean it shows one thing if you have to  leave your country because of war  because bombs explode next to you and  you want to save the life of your  children no walls can stop you so  instead of investing money into walls we  should welcome these people and benefit  from them that makes much more sense in  my opinion and of course on the other  side we also have to look into the  causes the root causes why these people  leave their country and in the case of  Syria it's obviously not easy but we  have to make sure that together with  Russia together with Iran we come to a  solution that we had an interim  government for for Syria in order to  stop that war and then fight together  against Isis thanks a lot mr. Jose  Malcolm
 

